WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.981
Review sheet.

2
00:00:01.261 --> 00:00:10.584
A language model factors a sequence probability into next-token conditionals (exact), then limits what each conditional sees (the approximation).

3
00:00:10.864 --> 00:00:15.152
Counting and normalizing rows is the maximum likelihood estimate.

4
00:00:15.432 --> 00:00:19.976
Average NLL is the loss; log V is the uniform baseline (3.

5
00:00:20.256 --> 00:00:25.461
296 for 27 tokens), and the counted bigram reaches about 2.

6
00:00:25.741 --> 00:00:27.747
454 on the names.

7
00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:34.320
Smoothing adds pseudo-counts to avoid infinite loss on unseen events, at a small cost in training loss.

8
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:45.587
A one-hot times a matrix selects a row; softmax of learned logits recovers the counts; the gradient of NLL with respect to logits is softmax minus one-hot.

9
00:00:45.867 --> 00:00:50.475
Always check rows sum to 1, and always say which data a loss was measured on.
